# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sample documents — NOT COMMITTED BY DEFAULT
#
# The files at the repo root are real internal enterprise documents. At least
# one (FROGSLEAP_BUSINESS LICENSE.pdf) contains personal data: national ID
# numbers, dates of birth, and home addresses of named individuals. Others
# contain commercial pricing.
#
# They are therefore excluded from git so that pushing this repository —
# especially to a public remote — cannot disclose them. The pipeline reads
# them in place from the repo root; nothing depends on them being tracked.
#
# `samples/MANIFEST.json` IS committed: it records each file's name, size,
# SHA-256 and detected type, so the corpus is documented and verifiable
# without distributing its contents.
#
# If this repository is private and its policy permits committing these
# documents, delete this block and run `git add` explicitly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.pdf
/*.docx
/*.xlsx
/*.pptx
/*.doc
/*.xls
/*.ppt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.so

# Project caches / model weights (redirected off the OS drive, never committed)
.cache/
*.pth
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Run artifacts — regenerated by `run` / `compare` / `inspect` / failure report
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep

# Local experiment artifacts. The question, config and conclusions ARE
# committed (README.md / config.yaml / results.json / observations.md);
# bulky per-run output is not.
experiments/**/outputs/
experiments/**/rendered/
experiments/**/*.png
experiments/**/*.jpg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# experiments/005_omnidocbench — OmniDocBench benchmark integration
#
# The evaluator and its Python 3.10/3.11 environment live OUTSIDE version
# control (an external dependency, per the integration design — see
# experiments/005_omnidocbench/README.md): cloned upstream code, a public
# dataset that runs to gigabytes, per-page predictions, and the full metric
# debug dumps the evaluator writes. What IS committed from a benchmark run is
# small and deliberate: run.py/prepare.py/evaluate.py, config.yaml, and each
# backend's report.md + metrics.json + runtime.json + run_metadata.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.external/
/.venv-omnidoc/
experiments/005_omnidocbench/dataset/
experiments/005_omnidocbench/predictions/*
!experiments/005_omnidocbench/predictions/.gitkeep
experiments/005_omnidocbench/logs/*
!experiments/005_omnidocbench/logs/.gitkeep
experiments/005_omnidocbench/results/**/predictions/
# prepare.py's own doc_extraction stage outputs, self-deleted when a run
# completes normally (see prepare.py --keep-runs) — ignored defensively in
# case a run is interrupted, or --keep-runs was used deliberately to
# spot-check a page's intermediates.
experiments/005_omnidocbench/results/**/_doc_extraction_runs/
experiments/005_omnidocbench/results/**/*_result.json
# The evaluator's own environment fingerprint — copied in by evaluate.py as
# run_summary.json / runtime_environment.json (its raw filenames are
# prefixed, e.g. predictions_quick_match_run_summary.json; matching both
# forms here since the exact name depends on match_method). Excluded
# because it embeds this machine's hostname (`uname`), which is personally
# identifying, not because the content itself is sensitive.
experiments/005_omnidocbench/results/**/*run_summary.json
experiments/005_omnidocbench/results/**/*runtime_environment.json
experiments/005_omnidocbench/kaggle/*.output.ipynb

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Test / lint
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.log
